{
  "case_id": "2010-09-1279",
  "document_hash": "679ef302e05d41d3019d65b742f775675f76399e9739dd395bf897bb95f2076c",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "679ef302e05d41d3019d65b742f775675f76399e9739dd395bf897bb95f2076c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-679ef302e05d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in Case 09-1279, Federal Communications Commission v. AT&T, Inc. Mr. Yang."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "679ef302e05d41d3019d65b742f775675f76399e9739dd395bf897bb95f2076c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-679ef302e05d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Isn't it true that there are contexts in the law in which the word \"personal\" is used to refer to a corporation? For example, you could refer to personal jurisdiction over a corporation, couldn't you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "679ef302e05d41d3019d65b742f775675f76399e9739dd395bf897bb95f2076c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-679ef302e05d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about -- what about personal appearances?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "679ef302e05d41d3019d65b742f775675f76399e9739dd395bf897bb95f2076c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-679ef302e05d-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, as an administrative matter, can the corporation make a FOIA objection on behalf of its employees?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "679ef302e05d41d3019d65b742f775675f76399e9739dd395bf897bb95f2076c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-679ef302e05d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, if an individual has been -- individual human being has been investigated by the FBI and a FOIA request is made for records related to that investigation, would the name of the individual not be turned over?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "679ef302e05d41d3019d65b742f775675f76399e9739dd395bf897bb95f2076c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-679ef302e05d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question in this case is whether any organization, including not only business corporations like AT&T but also nonprofit organizations and political associations, should be categorically excluded from protection under Exemption 7(C), such that this exemption will now offer less protection for privacy interests than the Constitution and the common law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "679ef302e05d41d3019d65b742f775675f76399e9739dd395bf897bb95f2076c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-679ef302e05d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that where the adjective means \"of or relating to\" a term that Congress has expressly defined, that definition should be applied, so long as it makes sense to do so in light of the text and structure of the statute as a whole."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Project on Government Oversight",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "679ef302e05d41d3019d65b742f775675f76399e9739dd395bf897bb95f2076c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-679ef302e05d-0001-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Klineberg, you have read the brief of the Project on Government Oversight, where they give dozens and dozens of examples to show that, overwhelmingly, \"personal\" is used to describe an individual, not an artificial being."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "679ef302e05d41d3019d65b742f775675f76399e9739dd395bf897bb95f2076c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-679ef302e05d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What would be similar to\nmedical files and such, under Exemption 6, that uses the\nsame phrase, \"unwanted invasion on personal privacy\"?\nSo what would your reading do to Exemption 6, and how\nwould we create or even make sense of Exemption 6?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "679ef302e05d41d3019d65b742f775675f76399e9739dd395bf897bb95f2076c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-679ef302e05d-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If there are no further questions, I urge\nthat the -- that the Third Circuit be affirmed. Thank\nyou."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "AT&T",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "679ef302e05d41d3019d65b742f775675f76399e9739dd395bf897bb95f2076c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-679ef302e05d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "AT&T appears to have changed or at least\nmodified its position somewhat from the position\narticulated at page 14 of its brief. There AT&T\nsays, \"By expressly defining the noun 'person' to\ninclude corporations, Congress necessarily defined the\nadjective form of that noun -- 'personal' -- also to\ninclude corporations.\""
    },
    {
